  <section xml:id="sec-grip-method-four-grips-alt-fingerings">
    <title>Alternative fingerings of the four grips on the chromatic button accordion</title>

    <p>
      The grids below show <em>alternative fingerings</em> for the four important grips. On the chromatic button accordion. Buttons in column 4 and 5 on the treble keyboard are duplicates, which enables alternative fingerings of identical notes. This is particularly important where chords are at the exteme left or right of the keyboard.
    </p>

    <figure xml:id="fig-gm-all-four-alt">
      <caption>(The Lydian Dominant grip is a maj7 voicing with a flattened 5th)</caption>
      <sidebyside widths="18% 18% 18% 18% 18%" margins="2%">

